```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• `1result.sql` mis‑labels “possible injury” (injury_severity = 4) as a fatality, so its fatality / injury counts are incorrect.  
• `0result.sql` derives injuries simply as “all persons minus fatalities”, which also counts un‑injured occupants and therefore over‑states the injury total.  
• `2result.sql` keeps the official fatality count from `number_of_fatalities` and builds the injury count from the PERSON file using injury_severity IN (2,3,4,5), i.e. all non‑fatal injury codes—so its casualty figures are consistent with FARS coding rules, making it the only numerically correct query of the three.